# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide demonstrates a minimal working example of the `qiskit-paulice` package. We use [spacetime Pauli checks](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) to detect errors during execution of a Clifford circuit, then postselect only samples for which no error was detected. For a more explanatory end-to-end workflow that quantifies the fidelity improvement, see the [in-depth tutorial](/tutorials/spacetime-codes).\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng gabay na ito ang isang minimal na gumaganang halimbawa ng package na `qiskit-paulice`. Gumagamit tayo ng [spacetime Pauli checks](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) para madetect ang mga error habang tumatakbo ang isang Clifford circuit, tapos pinipili lang natin ang mga sample na walang natukoy na error (postselection). Para sa mas detalyadong end-to-end na workflow na sumusukat sa pagbuti ng fidelity, tingnan ang [malalimang tutorial](/tutorials/spacetime-codes).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Workflow steps**\n"
"1. Prepare the inputs: a Clifford payload circuit, the target/ancilla qubits to host checks, and a noise model.\n"
"2. Find good spacetime Pauli checks and add them to the circuit.\n"
"3. Sample the checked circuit.\n"
"4. Postselect only the samples for which no error was detected.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga hakbang ng workflow**\n"
"1. Ihanda ang mga input: isang Clifford payload circuit, ang mga target/ancilla qubit na magho-host ng mga check, at isang noise model.\n"
"2. Maghanap ng magagandang spacetime Pauli checks at idagdag ang mga ito sa circuit.\n"
"3. I-sample ang circuit na may checks.\n"
"4. I-postselect lang ang mga sample na walang natukoy na error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Prepare the inputs {#1-prepare-the-inputs}"
msgstr "1. Ihanda ang mga input {#1-prepare-the-inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`add_pauli_checks` takes a Clifford **circuit** ending in measurements (or, with the `stabilizers` kwarg, one with no measurements, as in the [spacetime codes guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice/guides/low-overhead-error-detection-using-spacetime-codes)), the **target qubits** that will be used to implement checks, and a **noise model** used to score candidate checks. Here we build a shallow random Clifford circuit, lay it out on a 1D chain of physical qubits on `ibm_boston`, pair each payload qubit with a neighboring ancilla (so a check needs no SWAP gates), and infer a rough depolarizing noise model from backend benchmark data.\n"
msgstr "Ang `add_pauli_checks` ay kumukuha ng isang Clifford **circuit** na nagtatapos sa mga measurement (o, gamit ang `stabilizers` kwarg, isang walang measurement, tulad ng sa [spacetime codes guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice/guides/low-overhead-error-detection-using-spacetime-codes)), ang **mga target qubit** na gagamitin para ipatupad ang mga check, at isang **noise model** na ginagamit para i-score ang mga kandidatong check. Dito, gumagawa tayo ng mababaw na random Clifford circuit, inilalatag ito sa 1D chain ng mga pisikal na qubit sa `ibm_boston`, ipinapares ang bawat payload qubit sa katabing ancilla (para hindi na kailangan ng SWAP gates ang check), at tinatantya ang magaspang na depolarizing noise model mula sa benchmark data ng backend.\n"

